    "answer": {
      "short": "For example, $\\frac12,\\ \\frac35,\\ \\frac58,\\ \\frac7{11}$.",
      "worked": "Work backwards from four fractions equivalent to $\\frac23$:\n$$\\frac23,\\quad\\frac46,\\quad\\frac69,\\quad\\frac8{12}.$$\nSubtract 1 from each numerator and denominator:\n$$\\frac{2-1}{3-1}=\\frac12,\\quad\\frac{4-1}{6-1}=\\frac35,$$\n$$\\frac{6-1}{9-1}=\\frac58,\\quad\\frac{8-1}{12-1}=\\frac7{11}.$$\nThese are four possible starting fractions.\nCheck the third example: $\\frac{5+1}{8+1}=\\frac69=\\frac23$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 40
